title: architect_intro
---
Architect: This basement is where I test movement and combat. If a hit looks wrong, turn on debug view and compare the boxes.
-> What is this place?
    <<jump architect_intro__1>>
-> Why show the debug boxes?
    <<jump architect_intro__2>>
-> Enough architecture for now.
===

title: architect_intro__1
---
Architect: The Kernel's maintenance rooms are down here. Enemy tests, boss patterns, breakable floors, unfinished shop rules. Most of it is still wired for inspection.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump architect_intro>>
-> Return to the room.
===

title: architect_intro__2
---
Architect: Keep the hitboxes, seeds, timers, graphs, and costs visible in debug mode. When a generated fight goes wrong, I want to see why.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump architect_intro>>
-> Return to the room.
===

title: generic_npc
---
Sandbox NPC: No named dialogue here yet. This is the fallback line.
-> Close.
===

title: hub_guide
---
Kernel Guide: Back in the Kernel. Doors use Interact. Double-tap Up is the fallback if you want to test it.
-> Why is Interact separate from Up?
    <<jump hub_guide__1>>
-> What should I test next?
    <<jump hub_guide__2>>
-> I would like to test dialog.
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
-> Back to the hub.
===

title: hub_guide__1
---
Kernel Guide: Up already aims, climbs, and flies. A single Up press should not open a door by accident. Use Interact for doors, shops, and conversations.
-> Ask another hub question.
    <<jump hub_guide>>
-> Return to movement.
===

title: hub_guide__2
---
Kernel Guide: Try the basement labs, then turn on debug mode. Check combo state, hitstun, invulnerability, health bars, and hurtboxes after any hit that looks wrong.
-> Ask another hub question.
    <<jump hub_guide>>
-> Return to movement.
===

title: merchant_seed
---
Merchant Prototype: Shop's open. Anything you can't afford is greyed out.
-> Buy Axe — 25g <<if can_afford(25)>>
    <<buy_item "axe" 25>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Health Cell — 8g <<if can_afford(8)>>
    <<buy_item "healthcell" 8>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Mana Cell — 8g <<if can_afford(8)>>
    <<buy_item "manacell" 8>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Gun-Sword — 35g <<if can_afford(35)>>
    <<buy_item "gunsword" 35>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Puppy-Slug Gun — 30g <<if can_afford(30)>>
    <<buy_item "puppysluggun" 30>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Bomb — 6g <<if can_afford(6)>>
    <<buy_item "bomb" 6>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Fireball — 40g <<if can_afford(40)>>
    <<buy_item "fireball" 40>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Blink — 45g <<if can_afford(45)>>
    <<buy_item "blink" 45>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Grapple — 45g <<if can_afford(45)>>
    <<buy_item "grapple" 45>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Buy Mark/Recall — 45g <<if can_afford(45)>>
    <<buy_item "markrecall" 45>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Sell Gun-Sword — 17g <<if condition("inventory.holds", "gunsword")>>
    <<sell_item "gunsword" 17>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Sell Axe — 12g <<if condition("inventory.holds", "axe")>>
    <<sell_item "axe" 12>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Sell Health Cell — 4g <<if condition("inventory.holds", "healthcell")>>
    <<sell_item "healthcell" 4>>
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Ask about refunds.
    <<jump merchant_seed__1>>
-> Leave.
===

title: merchant_seed__1
---
Merchant Prototype: Refunds stay available until a purchase changes a route, boss, or story flag. After that, the sale is final.
-> Back to shop stub.
    <<jump merchant_seed>>
-> Leave.
===

title: vault_keeper
---
Vault Keeper: Read the whole entry before you buy. Price, source, side effects, whether it persists, and whether I'll take it back are all listed.
-> Show the merchant plan.
    <<jump vault_keeper__1>>
-> What is ethical currency?
    <<jump vault_keeper__2>>
-> Not buying anything yet.
===

title: vault_keeper__1
---
Vault Keeper: The draft shop can grant abilities, refill health, open routes, set story flags, or show where an upgrade came from. Each choice carries its price.
-> Back to the vault menu.
    <<jump vault_keeper>>
-> Close the ledger.
===

title: vault_keeper__2
---
Vault Keeper: Check who paid for the upgrade. Some funding opens shortcuts and marks whatever you build with it. Other funding takes longer to earn but leaves a clean source record.
-> Back to the vault menu.
    <<jump vault_keeper>>
-> Close the ledger.
===

title: hub_guide__test
---
<<if visit_count("hub_guide__test") <= 1>>
    Kernel Guide: Test menu. Each option exercises one dialogue feature: markup, a command, a save-state query, or multi-line output.
<<else>>
    Kernel Guide: Test menu again. Pick another entry.
<<endif>>
-> Markup: ⟨shout⟩
    <<jump hub_guide__test_shout>>
-> Markup: ⟨whisper⟩
    <<jump hub_guide__test_whisper>>
-> Multi-line accumulation.
    <<jump hub_guide__test_multiline>>
-> Command: world.set_flag
    <<jump hub_guide__test_flag>>
-> Command: play_sfx
    <<jump hub_guide__test_sfx>>
-> Command: spawn_fireworks
    <<jump hub_guide__test_fireworks>>
-> Command: give_item
    <<jump hub_guide__test_item>>
-> Command: camera_zoom
    <<jump hub_guide__test_zoom>>
-> Command: spawn_chest
    <<jump hub_guide__test_chest>>
-> Function: boss_cleared
    <<jump hub_guide__test_boss>>
-> Function: visit_count
    <<jump hub_guide__test_visit>>
-> Function: quest_active
    <<jump hub_guide__test_quest>>
-> Condition: inventory.holds
    <<jump hub_guide__test_inv>>
-> Back to the main hub guide.
    <<jump hub_guide>>
===

title: hub_guide__test_shout
---
Kernel Guide: Next line uses shout markup. The bridge sets YarnPresentationCue.shout for this frame; camera and audio consumers can read it.
Kernel Guide: [shout]LOUD VOICE — CAMERA SHAKE HOOK FIRES NOW.[/shout]
Kernel Guide: Normal line. The shout cue clears on the next frame.
-> Back to test menu.
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
===

title: hub_guide__test_whisper
---
Kernel Guide: Next line uses whisper markup. The whisper cue drives the pitch and volume hooks.
Kernel Guide: [whisper]quiet voice — pitched-down audio hook would fire here[/whisper]
Kernel Guide: Normal line again.
-> Back to test menu.
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
===

title: hub_guide__test_multiline
---
Kernel Guide: Three lines follow with no options or Confirm press between them.
Kernel Guide: The bridge advances each PresentLine and joins them with paragraph breaks.
Kernel Guide: All three should be on one page. The option below comes after the third line.
-> Back to test menu.
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
===

title: hub_guide__test_flag
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "kernel_guide_demo_flag")>>
    Kernel Guide: The condition catalog reads world.flag_set(kernel_guide_demo_flag) = TRUE.
<<else>>
    Kernel Guide: The condition catalog reads world.flag_set(kernel_guide_demo_flag) = FALSE.
<<endif>>
Kernel Guide: condition() reads the world-fact domain directly. Toggle the flag, return to the menu, then open this test again and check the value.
-> Set the flag.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "kernel_guide_demo_flag" true>>
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
-> Clear the flag.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "kernel_guide_demo_flag" false>>
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
-> Back to test menu (no change).
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
===

title: hub_guide__test_sfx
---
Kernel Guide: Sending SfxMessage::Play for ui.notification.discovery.
<<play_sfx "ui.notification.discovery">>
Kernel Guide: That chime is ui.notification.discovery from sfx.bank. play_sfx accepts any registered clip id.
-> Back to test menu.
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
===

title: hub_guide__test_fireworks
---
Kernel Guide: Calling spawn_fireworks. Expect staggered explosion sprites and matching explosion audio.
<<spawn_fireworks>>
Kernel Guide: If the sequence is silent or all fires at once, inspect ExplosionRequest and FireworksRequest.
-> Back to test menu.
    <<jump hub_guide__test>>
===

